A medical system comprising:
 an image capture probe including a camera at a tip of the image capture probe; 
 a sensor system; and 
 a processor configured to:
 receive a true image from the camera of the image capture probe when the image capture probe is located within an anatomic region of a patient anatomy; 
 identify a position of the tip of the image capture probe based on information received from the sensor system; 
 identify a tissue structure in the true image; 
 identify a plurality of virtual tissue structures in a model of the anatomic region based on the position of the tip of the image capture probe; 
 compare the tissue structure to at least a portion of the plurality of virtual tissue structures to identify a best matched virtual tissue structure; and 
 perform a registration of the true image to the model of the anatomic region based on identification of the best matched virtual tissue structure to identify a virtual probe position for the tip of the image capture probe with respect to the model.

